@page "/tables/simple-table/loading-mode"

@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Switch
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.AdvancedTable.Components.Footers
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.Shared.Enums
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components
@using ViciOne.Ui.Blazor.Components.Tables.SimpleTable.Components.Columns

<h3>Loading modes</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    The table supports two loading modes:

    <strong>Virtualize</strong> renders only visible rows (efficient for large datasets),
    while <strong>Load All</strong> renders every row at once.

    Virtualization requires <code>MaximumHeight</code> to be set — without it the table has no bounded viewport and virtualization has no effect.

    Toggle below to switch.
</DescriptionBanner>

<h3>Range selection across both modes</h3>

<DescriptionBanner>
    Click a row, scroll well past it, then <kbd>Shift</kbd>-click another: every row in between is selected, in both
    loading modes. Under <strong>Virtualize</strong> the rows outside the viewport were never rendered, so the
    range is resolved by position and fetched in one go — which is why the selected count in the footer can far
    exceed the number of rows on screen.

    The footer is the feedback channel for that: a range can reach rows the viewport never shows, so a table
    offering range selection under virtualization wants a footer reporting the count.
</DescriptionBanner>

<div class="virtualize-wrapper">
    <div>Virtualize table</div>
    <Switch @bind-Value="_virtualize" />
</div>

<SimpleTable Items="s_items"
             Mode="@LoadingMode"
             SelectionMode="SelectionMode.Multiple"
             ItemIdSelector="item => item.Id"
             @bind-SelectedItems="_selectedItems"
             MaximumHeight="300px">
    <Footer>
        <TableFooter SelectedItemCount="_selectedItems.Count" />
    </Footer>
    <Columns>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Id" Title="Id">
            <CellContent>
                @context.Id
            </CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Key" Title="Key">
            <CellContent>
                @context.Key
            </CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Value" Title="Value">
            <CellContent>
                @context.Value
            </CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
        <SimpleTableTemplateColumn Id="Timestamp" Title="Timestamp">
            <CellContent>
                @context.Timestamp
            </CellContent>
        </SimpleTableTemplateColumn>
    </Columns>
</SimpleTable>
